WEBVTT

00:00:00.015 --> 00:00:02.739
Easy Fables. Part 6.

00:00:02.739 --> 00:00:04.128
The Two Goats.

00:00:04.128 --> 00:00:08.493
Two goats met in the middle of a very narrow bridge over a river.

00:00:08.493 --> 00:00:11.543
There was not enough room for them to pass each other.

00:00:11.543 --> 00:00:14.169
"Go back," said the first goat.

00:00:14.169 --> 00:00:15.685
"I was here first."

00:00:15.685 --> 00:00:18.764
"No, you go back," said the second.

00:00:18.764 --> 00:00:20.375
"I am older than you."

00:00:20.375 --> 00:00:22.531
Neither of them wanted to give way.

00:00:22.531 --> 00:00:25.398
They began to push each other with their heads.

00:00:25.398 --> 00:00:27.497
They pushed harder and harder.

00:00:27.497 --> 00:00:30.640
In the end, both of them fell into the river.

00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:33.718
Sometimes giving way is the wise thing to do.

00:00:33.718 --> 00:00:36.010
The Fisherman and the Little Fish.

00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:39.900
A fisherman worked all day and caught only one small fish.

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:42.439
"Please let me go," said the fish.

00:00:42.439 --> 00:00:44.868
"I am too small to make a good dinner.

00:00:44.868 --> 00:00:46.676
Put me back in the river.

00:00:46.676 --> 00:00:48.536
In a year I will be big.

00:00:48.536 --> 00:00:51.221
Then you can catch me again and eat well."

00:00:51.221 --> 00:00:52.867
The fisherman laughed.

00:00:52.867 --> 00:00:55.026
"I have you now," he said.

00:00:55.026 --> 00:00:58.758
"If I let you go, I may never see you again.

00:00:58.758 --> 00:01:03.489
A small fish today is better than a big fish that I may never catch."

00:01:03.489 --> 00:01:07.372
What you have now is worth more than what you only hope to get.

00:01:07.372 --> 00:01:09.066
The Stag at the Pool.

00:01:09.066 --> 00:01:11.375
A stag was drinking at a pool.

00:01:11.375 --> 00:01:13.521
He saw himself in the water.

00:01:13.521 --> 00:01:16.513
"What beautiful horns I have," he said.

00:01:16.513 --> 00:01:19.199
"But my legs are so thin and ugly.

00:01:19.199 --> 00:01:21.136
I do not like them at all."

00:01:21.136 --> 00:01:23.973
Just then some hunters came with their dogs.

00:01:23.973 --> 00:01:25.316
The stag ran.

00:01:25.316 --> 00:01:32.143
His thin legs carried him quickly across the open field, and soon he was far in front of the dogs.

00:01:32.143 --> 00:01:34.517
But then he ran into a forest.

00:01:34.517 --> 00:01:38.062
His beautiful horns were caught in the branches of a tree.

00:01:38.062 --> 00:01:41.267
He could not get free, and the dogs reached him.

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:43.951
"How foolish I was," he said.

00:01:43.951 --> 00:01:46.636
"The legs I did not like could have saved me.

00:01:46.636 --> 00:01:49.443
The horns I was so proud of have killed me."

00:01:49.443 --> 00:01:52.928
What is most useful is often not what looks best.

00:01:52.928 --> 00:01:54.870
The Travelers and the Tree.

00:01:54.870 --> 00:01:58.739
Two men were walking along a road on a very hot day.

00:01:58.739 --> 00:02:01.604
They were tired, and the sun was burning.

00:02:01.604 --> 00:02:04.703
Then they saw a big tree with wide branches.

00:02:04.703 --> 00:02:08.104
They lay down under it and rested in the cool shade.

00:02:08.104 --> 00:02:11.704
After a while, one of them looked up at the tree.

00:02:11.704 --> 00:02:14.718
"What a useless tree this is," he said.

00:02:14.718 --> 00:02:16.228
"It has no fruit.

00:02:16.228 --> 00:02:18.501
Nobody can eat anything from it."

00:02:18.501 --> 00:02:21.326
"How can you say that?" the tree answered.

00:02:21.326 --> 00:02:24.553
"At this very moment you are lying in my shade.

00:02:24.553 --> 00:02:26.427
And you call me useless?"

00:02:26.427 --> 00:02:29.618
Many people do not see the good things they are given.

00:02:29.618 --> 00:02:31.557
The Lark and Her Children.

00:02:31.557 --> 00:02:34.382
A lark had her nest in a field of corn.

00:02:34.382 --> 00:02:38.872
One day her children heard the farmer say, "The corn is ready.

00:02:38.872 --> 00:02:42.108
I will ask my neighbors to help me cut it tomorrow."

00:02:42.108 --> 00:02:44.236
The young birds were afraid.

00:02:44.236 --> 00:02:46.973
But their mother said, "Do not worry.

00:02:46.973 --> 00:02:48.984
We do not need to move yet."

00:02:48.984 --> 00:02:51.270
The next day no neighbors came.

00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:55.321
The farmer said, "I will ask my brothers to help me."

00:02:55.321 --> 00:02:58.062
Again the mother said, "We can stay."

00:02:58.062 --> 00:03:00.033
The brothers did not come.

00:03:00.033 --> 00:03:05.298
Then the farmer said to his son, "Tomorrow we will cut the corn ourselves."

00:03:05.298 --> 00:03:07.999
"Now we must go," said the lark.

00:03:07.999 --> 00:03:12.709
"When a man decides to do the work himself, it will really be done."

00:03:13.324 --> 00:03:16.427
If you want something done, do it yourself.
